# ============================================================
# Killstreak - ignored paths
#
# NOTE: `git` is not currently installed in this environment, so this file is
# inert until the repository is initialised (`git init`). It is committed here so
# the intent is recorded rather than rediscovered.
# ============================================================

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# NOT ignored on purpose: package-lock.json. It pins vite and esbuild, which is
# what makes the build reproducible. Commit it.

# Build output. Regenerated by `npm run build`; vite.config.js sets outDir: 'dist'
# with emptyOutDir: true, so the directory is disposable by construction and is
# deliberately not kept in the tree.
dist/

# Vite / esbuild caches
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Environment files - never commit secrets
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.local

# Editor and OS cruft
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~

# ============================================================
# Deliberately NOT ignored
#
# Being explicit because these look like generated/scratch artefacts but are
# load-bearing:
#
#   scratch/         The verifier suite (21 scripts), scratch/slices/*.json
#                    manifests and scratch/phase7_dom_probe.js all live here.
#                    It is part of the project, not a dump.
#
#   scratch/backup/  The pre-phase snapshots are read directly by 12 of the suite
#                    scripts: verify_cutscenes, verify_domrefs, verify_hud,
#                    verify_inventory, verify_splice, verify_splice_cutscenes,
#                    verify_splice_renderers, verify_sword_strategy, verify_systems,
#                    verify_utils, verify_slice (which resolves the .bak paths named
#                    inside scratch/slices/*.json) and validate_phase1. verify_i18n
#                    reads scratch/backup/obsolete/js-i18n.js the same way. They are
#                    also the only copies of the pre-refactor state, so ignoring them
#                    would leave the suite unrunnable on a fresh clone.
#
#   .github/         Project agent rules (agents/KILLSTREAK.agent.md) - authored,
#                    not generated.
#
#   data/            The 31 .js data scripts are LIVE - src/main.js imports them.
#                    They are source, not generated output. Do not ignore this
#                    folder and do not regenerate it. (The .json siblings that used
#                    to sit beside them were stale and are deleted; the
#                    authoritative data is src/**/*.data.json. See
#                    critical_findings.stale-data-drift.)
#
#   js/              The legacy core is still live: entities.js holds Player,
#                    game.js holds Game, main.js is the composition root.
#
#   *.bak / *.orig   Do NOT add a blanket *.bak rule. 21 .bak files live under
#                    scratch/backup/ and verify_slice resolves the paths named in
#                    scratch/slices/*.json to read their bodies back. Scope any
#                    such rule tightly, or skip it.
# ============================================================
